{
  "code": "POLSC-PHD",
  "reviewed": "2026-10-23",
  "summary": "You complete the program courses (POLISCI 450A and 450B, a political theory course, a research design course, each for 5 units, and POLISCI 480 with an S) and the courses for a first, second and third field, all letter graded. With Comparative Politics as your first field, your research design course must be POLISCI 440C. Every course needs a B or better, and first- and second-field courses an A- or better. That your fields differ, the self-designed third field, the prospectus, teaching, the first-field exam and field paper, the oral exam and the dissertation are checked by hand.",
  "program": {
    "minGrade": "B",
    "why": "Grading: \"Students are required to earn grades of B or better in all courses take each term. While a B is the minimum required grade for all classes, all students must earn a minimum grade of A- for courses taken to fulfill first and second field requirements.\" Letter grades are set per rule, since POLISCI 480 is graded S."
  },
